{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Database access does not mean access to every piece of data is needed. A developer checking order status does not necessarily need settlement amounts or internal notes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I tested that separation in QueryPie ACP: orders and settlements in the same database, with the developer allowed to keep querying orders but denied access to settlements."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Can normal queries continue while only protected tables are restricted?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " I ran the same SQL in DBeaver before and after applying the policy."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Confirming Settlements Are Initially Readable"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Using Orders Control Lab in QueryPie ACP Community 11.6.7, I added settlement_details beside orders and inserted three fictional settlement IDs, order IDs, amounts, and internal notes. No actual customer or company settlement data was used."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Demo Developer connected through QueryPie using DBeaver. The registered database account could read both tables."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Before creating the policy, the settlement query returned records 9001–9003 with amounts and notes. This became the baseline for comparison."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/01.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 1. Before the policy, the developer can read settlement amounts and internal notes.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 1. Before the policy, the developer can read settlement amounts and internal notes."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Creating a Policy to Protect the Settlement Table"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Under Databases → Policies → Data Access, I clicked Create Policy and created Orders Lab - Settlement Access for Orders Control Lab."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/02.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 2. Creating a Data Access policy for the lab connection.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 2. Creating a Data Access policy for the lab connection."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In Add Rule List, I selected orders_control and settlement_details. To protect the whole table, I left Column Name unspecified and added no exceptions under Allowed Users."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/03.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 3. Selecting the settlement table to protect within the same database.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 3. Selecting the settlement table to protect within the same database."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The saved rule listed the database and table. Orders was not included. The list made it easy to verify exactly which data was restricted."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/04.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 4. Rule registered for orders_control.settlement_details.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 4. Rule registered for orders_control.settlement_details."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The Same SQL Now Blocks Settlement Access"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Back in DBeaver, I ran the identical settlement query. Instead of data, it returned a message asking me to check access permissions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It named the table: ‘You don't have permission to access the table 'orders_control.settlement_details'.’ Settlement data visible before the policy was no longer returned."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/05.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 5. Identical settlement SQL is blocked, with the restricted table named in the message.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 5. Identical settlement SQL is blocked, with the restricted table named in the message."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I changed neither DBeaver’s connection settings nor the database account’s SELECT privilege. QueryPie’s newly added Data Access rule governed the proxied query."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Even users allowed to connect can be limited to tables needed for their work. This made post-connection privilege design concrete from an adoption perspective."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Order Queries Continue as Usual"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "After the block, I queried IDs and statuses from orders over the same DBeaver connection. Orders 4001 and 4003 were PENDING; 4002 was DELIVERED, as expected."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/06.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 6. All three orders remain readable after restricting settlements.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 6. All three orders remain readable after restricting settlements."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "This was my favorite part of the exercise."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " Developers could continue checking order status while settlement data was protected separately. They kept DBeaver; administrators selected the protected table in QueryPie."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This brought shared databases across departments to mind. Defining which tables can be read, in addition to whether a connection is allowed, enables finer task-based data boundaries."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Blocked Queries Are Recorded Too"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the policy’s Logs tab, the recent query appeared as Access Denied, attributed to Demo Developer and settlement_details with its execution time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/07.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 7. Blocked settlement access logged with the user and execution time.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 7. Blocked settlement access logged with the user and execution time."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opening Query Details showed connection, table, user, and the settlement SQL from DBeaver. Rows was 0."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "attrs": {
        "src": "/assets/content/acp-lab-notes/table-access-control/08.webp",
        "alt": "Screen 8. The restricted table and actual SQL appear together in the detail view.",
        "title": null,
        "width": "100%",
        "height": null,
        "caption": "Screen 8. The restricted table and actual SQL appear together in the detail view."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If someone asks why a query failed, these records provide an explanation: identify the user and time, inspect the targeted table in SQL, and explain the policy outcome."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Defining Data Boundaries After Granting a Connection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "One small rule made the difference clear. Before it, both orders and settlements were readable. Afterward, settlements were blocked while orders remained available."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Part 7 masked parts of contacts; here I restricted a whole table. Different protection methods can fit different data and tasks."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            }
          ],
          "text": "Keep necessary work moving while protecting data people do not need to see."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " With Data Access, I configured that distinction in the administrator view, verified it in the user’s tool, and reviewed its logs. It is a feature I would show someone designing task-specific database privileges."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
